所以是菲利斯对阵迈克尔，但接着鲍勃·万斯也扮成圣诞老人出现了。

622
00:27:20.120 --> 00:27:20.420
That's right.
没错。

623
00:27:20.620 --> 00:27:22.180
We end up having three Santas.
我们最后竟然有了三个圣诞老人。

624
00:27:22.180 --> 00:27:27.820
But Phyllis has such a great talking head about being Santa.
但菲利斯关于扮演圣诞老人的单人访谈真的太棒了。

625
00:27:27.820 --> 00:27:31.040
I love it so much, and I feel like we need to hear it.
我太喜欢了，我觉得我们有必要听一听。

626
00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:33.400
I have been wanting to be Santa for years.
我好多年来一直想当圣诞老人。

627
00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:37.700
I believe I have the right temperament and the figure to do the job well.
我相信我有合适的脾气和身材把这份工作做好。

628
00:27:37.880 --> 00:27:42.240
I slipped a note to Jim 11 weeks ago, and he said I could do it.
我11周前给吉姆塞了张纸条，他说我可以干。

629
00:27:44.500 --> 00:27:51.970
Oh, it's been a long journey, but I'm Santa Claus.
哦，这一路走来不容易，但我现在是圣诞老人了。

630
00:27:52.490 --> 00:27:54.570
Aw, I love Santa Phyllis.
噢，我超爱圣诞老人菲利斯。

631
00:27:54.710 --> 00:27:55.230
I know.
我知道。

632
00:27:55.470 --> 00:27:57.070
Santa Phyllis is so sweet.
圣诞老人菲利斯太甜了。

633
00:27:57.590 --> 00:28:01.570
Well, you know, Jenna, all this talk about Santas on the set of The Office makes me think
话说回来，珍娜，在《办公室》片场聊了这么多圣诞老人，让我想起

634
00:28:01.570 --> 00:28:07.150
of a story I want to share about meeting someone who became a Santa's helper.
一个故事，我想分享一下关于遇到一个后来成为圣诞老人助手的人。

635
00:28:07.530 --> 00:28:12.190
And moms and dads out there, if you're listening, you might want to listen to this part first
各位爸爸妈妈们，如果你们在听的话，在跟家人和任何小朋友分享这部分之前，

636
00:28:12.190 --> 00:28:14.490
before you share it with your family and any little ears.
你们可能想先听听这个。

637
00:28:15.130 --> 00:28:16.030
Yes, good point.
对，说得好。

638
00:28:16.290 --> 00:28:20.990
You might be driving to your holiday stuff right now, and that's a good tip, Ange.
你们现在可能正开车去参加节日活动，这是个好提醒，安吉。

639
00:28:20.990 --> 00:28:24.510
Yeah, it's a great story, and I'm excited to share it.
对，这是个很棒的故事，我很高兴能分享它。

640
00:28:24.910 --> 00:28:26.050
This is the best story.
这绝对是最好的故事。

641
00:28:26.190 --> 00:28:32.150
When you were making your Hallmark Christmas movie in Vancouver, you left me a message
当你在温哥华拍你的 Hallmark 圣诞电影时，你给我留了一条语音留言，

642
00:28:32.890 --> 00:28:35.930
that I was like, you have to tell this on the podcast sometime.
当时我就觉得，你以后一定要在播客里讲讲这个。

643
00:28:36.150 --> 00:28:38.370
So I feel like this is the perfect time.
所以我觉得现在是最佳时机。

644
00:28:38.370 --> 00:28:38.870
I agree.
我同意。

645
00:28:39.230 --> 00:28:43.570
So yeah, like Jenna said, I was working on my Hallmark Christmas movie, and you know,
所以，是的，就像珍娜说的，我当时正在拍我的 Hallmark 圣诞电影，你知道的，

646
00:28:43.710 --> 00:28:47.350
to get to the set, the location was about an hour from where I was staying.
为了去片场，拍摄地点离我住的地方大约有一个小时的车程。

647
00:28:47.350 --> 00:28:52.230
So every day, they would send a transportation driver that worked on the movie to drive me
所以每天，他们都会派一个剧组的专职司机开车送我

648
00:28:52.230 --> 00:28:52.890
to the set.
去片场。

649
00:28:53.350 --> 00:28:56.590
And one of the guys that drove me was named Dan Cresswell.
其中一个送过我的司机叫丹·克雷斯韦尔。

650
00:28:57.310 --> 00:29:00.850
And when you have an hour drive, you get to know someone.
当你要坐一个小时的车时，你就会慢慢了解一个人。

651
00:29:00.970 --> 00:29:01.870
You start chatting.
你们开始聊天。

652
00:29:02.050 --> 00:29:05.770
And on one of our drives, I asked him, oh, are you going to go work on another movie?
然后在我们的一次车程中，我问他，哦，你要去拍另一部电影吗？

653
00:29:05.810 --> 00:29:09.630
Because a lot of the crew was saying they already had another job, another Christmas movie
因为许多剧组人员都在说他们已经找好了另一份工作，另一部圣诞电影

654
00:29:09.630 --> 00:29:10.170
lined up.
已经安排上了。

655
00:29:10.250 --> 00:29:14.750
And he said, no, I'm about to take my three-month yearly break.
他说，不，我准备开始我每年三个月的休假了。

656
00:29:15.350 --> 00:29:17.370
And I thought, three months off?
我想，休假三个月？

657
00:29:17.650 --> 00:29:19.050
I was so curious.
我太好奇了。

658
00:29:19.070 --> 00:29:21.710
I said, well, what do you do during these three months?
我说，那你这三个月都做些什么呢？

659
00:29:22.090 --> 00:29:24.570
And he said, well, I'm a professional Santa.
他说，嗯，我是一名职业圣诞老人。

660
00:29:24.870 --> 00:29:28.110
And from October to December, I start work as Santa.
从十月到十二月，我开始做圣诞老人。

661
00:29:28.490 --> 00:29:33.490
And then, I know you, Ange, you were like, I have so many questions.
然后，我懂你，安吉，你当时就像是，我有好多问题啊。

662
00:29:33.630 --> 00:29:34.190
Tell me more.
跟我多讲讲。

663
00:29:34.410 --> 00:29:34.770
I did.
我是真的这么做了。

664
00:29:34.970 --> 00:29:36.350
I was like, I have so many questions.
我当时就想，我有好多问题啊。

665
00:29:36.350 --> 00:29:37.590
And we have an hour car ride.
我们还要坐一个小时的车。

666
00:29:37.590 --> 00:29:38.690
So we're going to get into it.
所以我们要好好聊聊这个。

667
00:29:39.310 --> 00:29:43.070
First of all, lady, I had to ask him, how did this start?
首先，这位女士，我不得不问他，这一切是怎么开始的？

668
00:29:43.070 --> 00:29:46.470
How do you just kind of wake up one day and say, I'm going to be a Santa?
你怎么能有一天醒来就说，我要当个圣诞老人？

669
00:29:46.690 --> 00:29:48.290
Well, does he look like Santa?
那么，他长得像圣诞老人吗？

670
00:29:48.450 --> 00:29:50.310
Does he grow out a beard and everything?
他会留起胡子什么的吗？

671
00:29:50.610 --> 00:29:52.870
He does not look like a Santa at all.
他一点也不像圣诞老人。

672
00:29:53.010 --> 00:29:58.790
And he will be very quick to tell you, by the way, that all the Santas you see, they
顺便说一句，他会很快告诉你们，你们看到的所有的圣诞老人，他们

673
00:29:58.790 --> 00:30:00.010
are Santa's helpers.
都是圣诞老人的助手。

674
00:30:00.290 --> 00:30:01.810
They're not the real Santa.
他们不是真正的圣诞老人。

675
00:30:02.170 --> 00:30:05.730
They're all Santa's helpers for everyone listening out there.
对于收听节目的所有人来说，他们都是圣诞老人的助手。

676
00:30:05.890 --> 00:30:06.490
That's right.
没错。

677
00:30:06.850 --> 00:30:11.450
So all the kids listening out there, Dan wanted you to know that he's a Santa's helper.
所以所有收听节目的小朋友们，丹想让你们知道他是个圣诞老人助手。

678
00:30:12.150 --> 00:30:15.430
Because it's a busy season and Santa needs all the help he can get.
因为这是一个忙碌的季节，圣诞老人需要他能得到的所有帮助。

679
00:30:15.570 --> 00:30:15.930
That's right.
没错。

680
00:30:16.410 --> 00:30:21.450
So anyways, I'm like, but Dan, seriously, when did you start doing this?
所以不管怎样，我就想，但是丹，说真的，你是什么时候开始做这个的？

681
00:30:21.790 --> 00:30:24.890
He said, well, it all started about seven years ago.
他说，嗯，这一切始于大约七年前。

682
00:30:25.330 --> 00:30:28.010
I was earning extra money delivering pizzas.
我当时靠送外卖披萨赚点外快。

683
00:30:28.810 --> 00:30:30.070
And it was November.
那是十一月。

684
00:30:30.070 --> 00:30:32.990
And my son, Zachary, was 11 years old at the time.
我儿子扎卡里当时11岁。

685
00:30:33.170 --> 00:30:37.730
And he said, Dad, you should dress up as Santa when you deliver pizza.
他说，爸爸，你送披萨的时候应该扮成圣诞老人。

686
00:30:37.730 --> 00:30:39.610
I think that would be really fun.
我觉得那会非常有趣。

687
00:30:39.610 --> 00:30:41.530
And maybe you'd get better tips.
而且说不定能收到更多小费。

688
00:30:42.610 --> 00:30:43.790
That's smart kid.
真是个聪明的孩子。

689
00:30:43.890 --> 00:30:44.770
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

690
00:30:45.110 --> 00:30:46.630
And Dan kind of laughed.
丹笑了一下。

691
00:30:46.690 --> 00:30:47.750
And then he thought about it.
然后他考虑了一下。

692
00:30:47.850 --> 00:30:49.770
And then he was at Walmart.
接着他在沃尔玛。

693
00:30:49.770 --> 00:30:51.590
And there was a Santa suit for $50.
那里有一套50美元的圣诞老人服。

694
00:30:51.730 --> 00:30:53.550
So he decided to give it a go.
于是他决定尝试一下。

695
00:30:53.750 --> 00:30:59.550
He said his very first pizza delivery dressed as Santa, a dad opened the door and his little
他说他第一次扮成圣诞老人去送披萨时，一位爸爸开门，他的小

696
00:30:59.550 --> 00:31:00.990
girls were standing there with him.
女儿们正和他站在一起。

697
00:31:01.610 --> 00:31:04.030
And they lost their minds.
然后她们激动得不得了。

698
00:31:04.030 --> 00:31:07.870
They were so excited that Santa had come and brought them pizza.
她们太兴奋了，因为圣诞老人竟然来给她们送披萨。

699
00:31:08.150 --> 00:31:13.830
And the dad said, would it be OK if I take a picture of you with my daughters for Christmas?
那位爸爸说，我可以为了圣诞节给你和我的女儿们拍张照片吗？

700
00:31:14.330 --> 00:31:15.330
Dan said, sure.
丹说，当然可以。

701
00:31:15.490 --> 00:31:17.790
And he said the whole family was so thrilled.
他说全家人都兴奋极了。

702
00:31:18.090 --> 00:31:20.790
And after that, he did get a nice little tip.
在那之后，他还真的收到了一小笔不错的消费。

703
00:31:20.810 --> 00:31:24.230
And he thought, hmm, maybe there's something to this.
他心想，嗯，也许这行得通。

704
00:31:24.370 --> 00:31:30.270
He said that even as he would drive around town delivering pizzas in a Santa suit, people
他说，甚至当他穿着圣诞老人服装开车在城里送披萨时，人们

705
00:31:30.270 --> 00:31:31.470
would honk and wave.
也会按喇叭并向他挥手。

706
00:31:32.190 --> 00:31:34.770
They'd want to take their picture like through the car window.
他们甚至想透过车窗给他拍照。

707
00:31:35.330 --> 00:31:36.350
And he loved it.
而他非常喜欢这种感觉。

708
00:31:36.410 --> 00:31:39.630
And he told his wife, maybe I could do this as an actual business.
他告诉妻子，也许他可以把这当成一门真正的生意来做。

709
00:31:40.610 --> 00:31:43.410
He didn't know anything about it or how to go about it.
他对这一行一无所知，也不知道该如何着手。

710
00:31:43.630 --> 00:31:45.330
Lady, he Googled.
女士，他可是会用谷歌搜索的。

711
00:31:45.810 --> 00:31:48.530
He was a Santa who Googled?
他是一个会用谷歌的圣诞老人？

712
00:31:48.690 --> 00:31:49.130
Yes.
是的。

713
00:31:49.350 --> 00:31:51.810
He said he found a Santa school in Vancouver.
他说他在温哥华找到了一所圣诞老人学校。

714
00:31:52.310 --> 00:31:54.930
It was a four-day course, Friday through Monday.
那是一个为期四天的课程，从周五到周一。

715
00:31:55.350 --> 00:31:59.270
You get to learn how to become a professional Santa in marketing, et cetera.
你可以学习如何成为一名专业的圣诞老人，包括市场营销等等。

716
00:31:59.750 --> 00:32:05.130
And after that, he got a job as a Santa for Cabela's, which is very similar to like our
在那之后，他在 Cabela's 找到了一份圣诞老人的工作，这非常类似于我们的

717
00:32:05.130 --> 00:32:06.110
Bass Pro Shop.
巴斯户外商城。

718
00:32:06.410 --> 00:32:06.750
OK.
好的。

719
00:32:07.170 --> 00:32:08.890
And he worked there for two years.
他在那里工作了两年。

720
00:32:09.090 --> 00:32:10.910
He kind of did some highlighting at the mall.
他还在商场里做过一些高光亮相。

721
00:32:11.030 --> 00:32:13.970
But he really wanted to start his own Santa business.
但他真的很想创办自己的圣诞老人业务。

722
00:32:14.330 --> 00:32:15.450
This was his dream.
这是他的梦想。

723
00:32:16.550 --> 00:32:21.650
And his boss at the Cabela place got him a much better Santa suit.
他在 Cabela's 的老板给他弄了一套好得多的圣诞老人服。

724
00:32:22.530 --> 00:32:27.190
And he was like, ooh, I'm going to need all the Santa gear if I'm going to make this my
他当时就想，哦，如果我要把这变成我自己的生意，

725
00:32:27.190 --> 00:32:27.710
own business.
我将需要所有的圣诞老人装备。

726
00:32:27.710 --> 00:32:29.650
And I might need one or two more suits.
而且我可能还需要一两套更多的衣服。

727
00:32:29.790 --> 00:32:32.270
So he asked her, where do you get your Santa suits?
于是他问她，你是在哪里买到这些圣诞老人服的？

728
00:32:32.390 --> 00:32:33.110
And she said, uh-uh.
而她说，呃-嗯。

729
00:32:33.210 --> 00:32:33.950
I'm not telling you.
我才不告诉你呢。

730
00:32:33.950 --> 00:32:37.790
Why wouldn't she give up the details about where to get a good Santa suit?
为什么她不肯透露在哪里能买到优质的圣诞老人服呢？

731
00:32:37.970 --> 00:32:41.030
I guess she's the go-to for good Santa suits in Vancouver.
我猜她是温哥华优质圣诞老人服的首选供货人。

732
00:32:41.030 --> 00:32:42.670
And she didn't want to give up her source.
她不想泄露自己的进货渠道。

733
00:32:43.590 --> 00:32:44.030
Wow.
哇。

734
00:32:44.270 --> 00:32:44.730
I know.
我知道。

735
00:32:44.930 --> 00:32:47.090
So he really had to mom detective it.
所以他真的不得不像妈妈侦探一样去查探。

736
00:32:47.610 --> 00:32:51.150
He joined a bunch of online communities of working Santas.
他加入了许多在职圣诞老人的在线社群。

737
00:32:51.290 --> 00:32:53.870
He found a site called HireSanta.com.
他找到了一个叫做 HireSanta.com 的网站。

738
00:32:54.050 --> 00:32:56.590
I guess it was featured on the TV show Shark Tank.
我猜它曾在电视节目《创智赢家》中亮相过。

739
00:32:57.010 --> 00:32:58.530
And you want to know the best part?
你想知道最棒的部分是什么吗？

740
00:32:58.650 --> 00:33:00.770
He finally found where to get a good Santa suit.
他终于找到了在哪里可以买到一套好的圣诞老人服。

741
00:33:01.150 --> 00:33:01.410
Where?
在哪里？

742
00:33:01.970 --> 00:33:04.650
Adele Hollywood Costumes here in Los Angeles.
就在我们洛杉矶的阿黛尔好莱坞服装店。

743
00:33:05.150 --> 00:33:05.670
Oh.
哦。

744
00:33:05.930 --> 00:33:06.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

745
00:33:06.730 --> 00:33:11.850
He said he has two suits, the Coca-Cola Santa suit and the traditional Santa suit.
他说他有两套衣服，一套是可口可乐圣诞老人服，另一套是传统圣诞老人服。

746
00:33:12.030 --> 00:33:14.290
They run about $1,400 each.
它们每套大约要 1400 美元。

747
00:33:14.510 --> 00:33:14.810
Whoa.
哇。

748
00:33:15.310 --> 00:33:15.630
Yeah.
是的。

749
00:33:15.830 --> 00:33:17.390
But they're really nice, he said.
但他说它们真的很棒。

750
00:33:17.510 --> 00:33:19.110
And they last a long time.
而且非常耐穿。

751
00:33:19.250 --> 00:33:20.550
But that wasn't it.
但事情并非如此。

752
00:33:20.630 --> 00:33:22.050
Now he needed a good beard.
现在他需要一副好胡子。

753
00:33:22.230 --> 00:33:23.250
He does not have a beard.
他没有胡子。

754
00:33:23.450 --> 00:33:24.930
He has short brown hair.
他留着短短的棕色头发。

755
00:33:25.130 --> 00:33:26.150
He needed a beard.
他需要一副胡子。

756
00:33:26.270 --> 00:33:27.390
He needed the full look.
他需要整体的造型。

757
00:33:28.010 --> 00:33:30.410
The first beard he bought was in California.
他买的第一副胡子是在加利福尼亚买的。

758
00:33:30.410 --> 00:33:33.290
It was made from real hair and cost $1,500.
那是用真发做的，花了 1,500 美元。

759
00:33:34.230 --> 00:33:34.670
Wow.
哇。

760
00:33:34.970 --> 00:33:35.150
Yeah.
对。

761
00:33:35.430 --> 00:33:39.070
But it didn't hold up as well as he liked when kids would tug on it.
但当小孩子们拉扯它时，它不像他希望的那样经久耐用。

762
00:33:39.190 --> 00:33:40.710
Because he said they tug on your beard.
因为他说小孩子们会拽你的胡子。

763
00:33:41.110 --> 00:33:41.330
Okay.
好吧。

764
00:33:41.330 --> 00:33:49.130
So then through this community of Santas, he found a lady that makes handmade beards in
于是，通过这个圣诞老人社群，他找到了一位在

765
00:33:49.130 --> 00:33:51.810
China using yak hair.
中国用牦牛毛手工制作胡子的女士。

766
00:33:52.230 --> 00:33:52.830
Wow.
哇。

767
00:33:53.210 --> 00:33:53.530
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

768
00:33:53.710 --> 00:33:56.310
He said it's the best Santa beard out there.
他说这是现存最棒的圣诞老人胡子。

769
00:33:56.510 --> 00:34:00.390
They average around $900 to $1,000 Canadian.
它们的价格平均在 900 到 1,000 加元左右。

770
