when I was interning on Conan and it couldn't be more different.
那是我在柯南的节目实习的时候，简直有着天壤之别。

933
00:40:20.730 --> 00:40:21.910
But I want to tell you.
但我很想告诉你。

934
00:40:22.850 --> 00:40:23.990
So here I am.
当时的情况是这样的。

935
00:40:24.130 --> 00:40:25.250
I'm in my early 20s.
我才二十出头。

936
00:40:25.250 --> 00:40:28.930
I'm interning on Conan O'Brien when they used to tape at 30 Rockefeller Center.
我在柯南·奥布莱恩的节目组实习，当时他们还在洛克菲勒中心30号录制节目。

937
00:40:29.530 --> 00:40:33.330
And it's the day before the Macy's Day Parade.
那是梅西游行的前一天。

938
00:40:33.630 --> 00:40:37.710
And they close all these streets along the route, right?
他们会封锁游行沿线所有的街道，对吧？

939
00:40:38.330 --> 00:40:43.350
And it's in the morning and I'm walking to work and the street is closed.
那是早晨，我正走去上班，街道已经被封了。

940
00:40:43.690 --> 00:40:45.210
There's like no one on it.
街上几乎一个人也没有。

941
00:40:45.510 --> 00:40:51.890
And I see this man in a full suit, like a really nice suit with a nice coat.
然后我看到一个身穿全套西装的男子，是一套非常漂亮的西装，外面套着一件好大衣。

942
00:40:51.890 --> 00:41:00.110
And he is rollerblading with a briefcase through the street, just like zooming by.
他提着公文包，脚踩轮滑鞋在街上滑行，呼啸而过。

943
00:41:00.110 --> 00:41:05.010
And as he goes by me, I just said, oh, wow, that's so cool.
当他从我身边经过时，我忍不住说了一句，哇，太酷了。

944
00:41:05.110 --> 00:41:07.050
And he goes, my favorite day of the year.
他回答说，我一年中最喜欢的一天。

945
00:41:07.230 --> 00:41:09.110
I always skate to work on this day.
我每年这天都滑着轮滑去上班。

946
00:41:09.450 --> 00:41:10.670
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

947
00:41:12.370 --> 00:41:14.660
Isn't that funny?
是不是很有趣？

948
00:41:14.780 --> 00:41:15.140
Yes.
是的。

949
00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:24.980
And it was such a like visual, you know, to see this one lone skater in a suit in like an abandoned part of Manhattan.
那画面感太强了，你知道的，看到一个穿着西装的独行滑轮者，穿梭在曼哈顿空无一人的街道上。

950
00:41:25.280 --> 00:41:26.660
I'll never forget it.
我永远都不会忘记。

951
00:41:27.220 --> 00:41:27.440
Okay.
好的。

952
00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:33.720
So, lady, we have covered office Christmas memories, Santa gifts.
所以，女士们，我们已经聊过了办公室的圣诞记忆和圣诞老人的礼物。

953
00:41:33.720 --> 00:41:35.980
But there's one more thing I want to talk about.
但还有一件事我想谈谈。

954
00:41:36.520 --> 00:41:40.900
For me, another thing I love about the holidays is the music.
对我来说，我喜欢节日的另一个原因是音乐。

955
00:41:41.540 --> 00:41:41.960
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

956
00:41:42.200 --> 00:41:46.400
This is the time of year when you walk through the mall and you hear all the holiday songs playing.
每到这个时候，当你走过商场，就会听到到处都在播放节日歌曲。

957
00:41:46.620 --> 00:41:47.460
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

958
00:41:47.800 --> 00:41:52.340
And I wanted to ask the group, do you have a favorite holiday song?
我想问问大家，你们有没有最喜欢的节日歌曲？

959
00:41:52.480 --> 00:41:54.540
Like one that you look forward to hearing?
比如哪一首是你总是期待听到的？

960
00:41:54.860 --> 00:41:58.060
I think Bing Crosby's White Christmas does it for me.
我觉得平·克罗斯比的《白色圣诞》最对我的胃口。

961
00:41:58.180 --> 00:41:58.230
Oh, yes.
哦，对。

962
00:41:58.460 --> 00:41:58.780
Yes.
是的。

963
00:41:58.780 --> 00:42:07.680
Well, interestingly enough, Sam, I didn't know you were going to say that, but did you know that according to the Guinness Book of World Records,
有趣的是，萨姆，我本来不知道你会这么说，但你知道吗，根据《吉尼斯世界纪录大全》，

964
00:42:07.860 --> 00:42:13.220
White Christmas by Bing Crosby is not only the best-selling Christmas holiday single in the United States,
平·克罗斯比的《白色圣诞》不仅是美国最畅销的圣诞节日单曲，

965
00:42:13.220 --> 00:42:24.940
but it was also the best-selling single of all time since the advent of recorded music, with an estimated sales in excess of 50 million copies worldwide.
而且自从录音音乐诞生以来，它也是有史以来最畅销的单曲，全球预估销量超过 5000 万张。

966
00:42:25.160 --> 00:42:25.540
Wow.
哇。

967
00:42:25.540 --> 00:42:28.980
I believe it also hasn't not been on the charts since it came out.
我相信自从它发行以来，它就一直没有跌出过排行榜。

968
00:42:29.520 --> 00:42:29.840
Incredible.
太不可思议了。

969
00:42:30.620 --> 00:42:30.900
All right.
好吧。

970
00:42:31.160 --> 00:42:33.020
Cassie, do you have a favorite Christmas song?
凯西，你最喜欢哪首圣诞歌？

971
00:42:33.520 --> 00:42:33.960
Yes.
有。

972
00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:35.760
I like Wham's Last Christmas.
我喜欢威猛乐队的《去年圣诞节》。

973
00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:36.360
Oh!
哦！

974
00:42:36.360 --> 00:42:38.100
Oh, that's such a good one.
哦，那首歌真好听。

975
00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:40.220
That one charts the top often as well.
那首歌也经常登上排行榜前列。

976
00:42:40.340 --> 00:42:41.620
It's usually in the top five.
它通常都在前五名里。

977
00:42:41.960 --> 00:42:44.800
And I really did a deep dive on Christmas music.
我确实对圣诞音乐做了一番深入研究。

978
00:42:45.080 --> 00:42:48.080
I don't normally have these stats off the top of my head.
我平时脑子里可记不住这些数据。

979
00:42:48.340 --> 00:42:52.700
You know, it's so interesting because it's not so much just one song for me, but an album.
你知道，这很有趣，因为对我来说与其说是一首歌，不如说是一张专辑。

980
00:42:52.920 --> 00:42:53.240
Okay.
好的。

981
00:42:53.240 --> 00:42:55.860
So I love Elvis's Christmas album.
我很喜欢猫王的圣诞专辑。

982
00:42:56.020 --> 00:42:56.820
Oh, yes!
哦，对！

983
00:42:57.040 --> 00:42:57.920
It's so good.
太棒了。

984
00:42:58.240 --> 00:43:06.440
You know, his Silent Night, Holy Night, is really beautiful, but then he also has Santa Claus is Back in Town, and that's like a really fun one.
你知道，他的《平安夜，圣善夜》真的非常优美，但同时他还有一首《圣诞老人回小镇》，那首真的非常有趣。

985
00:43:06.560 --> 00:43:08.020
But I just love that album.
但我就是很爱那张专辑。

986
00:43:08.300 --> 00:43:13.780
It's interesting you say that, Angela, because my favorite Christmas song is also a favorite album.
安吉拉，你这么说很有意思，因为我最喜欢的圣诞歌曲也是一张最喜欢的专辑。

987
00:43:13.780 --> 00:43:21.320
I went through this phase where I got really into vinyl records, and my mom gave me her old record collection,
我经历过一个阶段，特别迷恋黑胶唱片，我妈妈把她以前的唱片收藏送给了我，

988
00:43:21.320 --> 00:43:26.060
and one of the records in the collection was a Frank Sinatra Christmas album.
收藏里的其中一张唱片就是弗兰克·辛纳屈的圣诞专辑。

989
00:43:26.700 --> 00:43:31.520
And I do bring out our little turntable and put it down by the Christmas tree.
我真的会搬出我们的小电唱机，把它放在圣诞树旁边。

990
00:43:31.720 --> 00:43:35.640
This is the first album that I play every season when we're decorating the tree.
这是每个季节我们装饰圣诞树时播放的第一张专辑。

991
00:43:35.640 --> 00:43:42.700
And the first song on the album is Frank Sinatra's Jingle Bells, and it's my favorite, and I'm going to play it.
专辑的第一首歌是弗兰克·辛纳屈的《铃儿响叮当》，这是我的最爱，我要把它放出来。

992
00:43:42.820 --> 00:43:43.240
Yay!
太棒了！

993
00:43:43.240 --> 00:43:52.920
I love those J-I-N-G-L-E bells.
我太喜欢那些铃儿 J-I-N-G-L-E 了。

994
00:43:53.140 --> 00:44:05.360
Oh, those holiday J-I-N-G-L-E-D-J-I-N-E-double-L-L-S.
哦，那些节日的 J-I-N-G-L-E-D-J-I-N-E-double-L-L-S。

995
00:44:11.980 --> 00:44:16.400
Jingle bells, jingle bells, jingle all the way.
铃儿响叮当，铃儿响叮当，一路响叮当。

996
00:44:16.400 --> 00:44:17.780
Oh, blue eyes.
哦，蓝眼睛。

997
00:44:17.980 --> 00:44:18.540
I know.
我知道。

998
00:44:18.840 --> 00:44:21.900
You just sing me right into Christmas, mister.
先生，你一唱歌就把我带进圣诞节了。

999
00:44:24.180 --> 00:44:25.640
Who are you right now?
你现在是谁啊？

1000
00:44:25.820 --> 00:44:26.580
I don't know.
我不知道。

1001
00:44:26.860 --> 00:44:27.700
I like it.
我喜欢。

1002
00:44:27.940 --> 00:44:33.440
You guys, you know, since we're talking holiday music, I have to give a shout out to our dear friend, Kate Flannery,
大家，你们知道的，既然我们在聊节日音乐，我必须得向我们的好朋友凯特·弗兰纳里致敬，

1003
00:44:33.660 --> 00:44:37.540
because she has a great Christmas album with Jane Lynch called A Swingin' Little Christmas.
因为她和简·林奇合作出了一张很棒的圣诞专辑，叫做《摇摆小圣诞》。g

1004
00:44:37.700 --> 00:44:38.300
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

1005
00:44:38.620 --> 00:44:39.920
And I also have that.
而且我也有那张。

1006
00:44:40.140 --> 00:44:40.860
It's so fun.
太有意思了。

1007
00:44:40.940 --> 00:44:43.020
Her show, she does a show this time of year.
她的演出，她每年这个时候都会有一场演出。

1008
00:44:43.020 --> 00:44:47.260
It's a super fun holiday show, and I just always love to give her a shout out.
那是一场超级有趣的节日演出，我总是很乐意向她致敬。

1009
00:44:48.020 --> 00:44:51.600
Well, we featured a lot of holiday music in our Office Christmas episodes.
嗯，我们在《办公室》的圣诞集里播放了很多节日音乐。

1010
00:44:51.840 --> 00:44:54.680
Angela, you played us Little Drummer Boy at the top of the episode.
安吉拉，你在节目开头为我们演奏了《小鼓手男孩》。g

1011
00:44:54.700 --> 00:45:01.260
We talked about when Dwight does his air guitar to Christmas Eve Sarajevo 1224.
我们聊到了德怀特对着《圣诞前夜萨拉热窝1224》弹空气吉他的那一幕。

1012
00:45:01.980 --> 00:45:07.580
That's the heavy metal medley of Christmas songs performed by the Trans-Siberian Orchestra.
那是跨西伯利亚管弦乐团演奏的圣诞歌曲重金属串烧。

1013
00:45:07.580 --> 00:45:18.020
But in general, Dunder Mifflin Christmas parties just love to bust out the karaoke and the microphones, and we did not limit ourselves to holiday songs.
但总的来说，邓德米夫林的圣诞派对就是喜欢尽情高歌卡拉OK和麦克风，而且我们并不局限于节日歌曲。

1014
00:45:18.420 --> 00:45:27.920
For example, in Benihana Christmas, when we had the dueling Christmas parties, we have Daryl on the keyboard and Kevin singing, and I thought we should listen.
例如，在《贝尼哈纳圣诞节》里，当我们在办对台圣诞派对时，达里尔弹键盘，凯文唱歌，我觉得我们应该听听看。

1015
00:45:27.920 --> 00:45:35.900
And I'm here to remind you of the mess you left when you went away.
而我在这里要提醒你，你离开时留下的烂摊子。

1016
00:45:36.140 --> 00:45:43.700
It's not fair to deny me of the cross I bear that you give to me.
剥夺我承受你施加给我的十字架的权力，这不公平。

1017
00:45:43.980 --> 00:45:48.240
You, you, you, you, you, you, you, you ought to know.
你，你，你，你，你，你，你，你本该知道。

1018
00:45:49.660 --> 00:45:50.880
There you go.
这不就成了。

1019
00:45:51.240 --> 00:45:51.880
Yeah, it worked.
对，成功了。

1020
00:45:52.080 --> 00:45:52.320
Yeah.
对。

1021
00:45:52.500 --> 00:45:52.960
Yes.
是的。

1022
00:45:53.140 --> 00:45:53.800
I love it.
我爱极了。

1023
00:45:53.800 --> 00:45:56.240
I remember it like I was there when Brian is coming.
我记得这事儿，就好像布莱恩来的时候我就在现场一样。

1024
00:45:56.360 --> 00:45:57.820
I was like, yo, yo, yo.
我当时就说，哟，哟，哟。

1025
00:45:58.820 --> 00:46:05.940
And of course, in Secret Santa, there's the time when Dwight and Andy sing Green Day's Boulevard of Broken DreaMs.
当然，在《秘密圣诞老人》那一集里，还有德怀特和安迪合唱绿日乐队的《迷失梦幻大道》的桥段。

1026
00:46:06.200 --> 00:46:08.060
Oh, I rewatched that one.
哦，我又看了一遍那一集。

1027
00:46:08.360 --> 00:46:12.060
We talked about that with Billy Joe Armstrong when we broke down that episode.
我们在拆解那一集时，和比利·乔·阿姆斯聊过这个。

1028
00:46:12.180 --> 00:46:13.740
Yeah, he was impressed with Ed.
对，他对埃德印象深刻。

1029
00:46:14.200 --> 00:46:15.260
Yes, he was.
是的，确实如此。

1030
00:46:15.820 --> 00:46:18.780
Well, the holidays just are not the same without the music.
嗯，没有音乐的节日就是感觉不对劲。

1031
00:46:18.780 --> 00:46:25.180
And last year, I heard a story about holiday music that I have been dying to share on the podcaSt.
去年，我听到一个关于节日音乐的故事，我一直渴望在播客里分享。

1032
00:46:25.450 --> 00:46:28.880
I have been waiting for us to do some sort of holiday-themed episode.
我一直在等我们做某种节日主题的节目。

1033
00:46:29.160 --> 00:46:30.460
And here I go.
现在我要讲了。

1034
00:46:30.860 --> 00:46:37.560
Now, I mentioned before that White Christmas by Bing Crosby was the best-selling holiday single in the United States.
我之前提过，平·克罗斯的《白色圣诞》是美国最畅销的节日单曲。

1035
00:46:37.560 --> 00:46:45.320
But starting in 1991, we started tracking digital downloads as well as copies sold.
但从1991年开始，我们开始追踪数字下载量以及售出的实体唱片数。

1036
00:46:45.520 --> 00:46:58.420
And as of November 25, 2016, the holiday single with the most digital downloads is Mariah Carey's 1994 track, All I Want for Christmas Is You.
截至2016年11月25日，数字下载量最高的节日单曲是玛丽亚·凯莉1994年的单曲《圣诞节我只想要你》。g

1037
00:46:58.800 --> 00:46:59.580
Let's listen.
我们来听听。

1038
00:46:59.820 --> 00:47:42.420
I love that song.
我喜欢那首歌。

1039
00:47:42.620 --> 00:47:44.140
It is a great song.
这真是一首好歌。

1040
00:47:44.140 --> 00:47:45.420
It's a great song.
这真是一首好歌。

1041
00:47:45.420 --> 00:47:47.680
It always makes me think of the end of that movie, Love.
它总是让我想起那部电影《真爱至上》的结尾。

1042
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:49.480
Actually, I love that song.
其实，我超爱这首歌。

1043
00:47:49.760 --> 00:47:52.940
Well, it's also the most popular holiday ringtone.
嗯，它也是最受欢迎的节日手机铃声。

1044
00:47:53.320 --> 00:47:53.640
Oh.
哦。

1045
00:47:54.320 --> 00:48:02.320
Okay, so for a very long time, Mariah Carey has had the number one spot on the Billboard Top 100 at the holidays.
好吧，所以在很长一段时间里，玛丽亚·凯莉在节假日的公告牌百强单曲榜上一直占据着榜首。

1046
00:48:02.840 --> 00:48:04.660
Like, she has been the reigning queen.
就像，她一直是当之无愧的女王。

1047
00:48:04.940 --> 00:48:12.840
And the number two spot, year after year, would go to Brenda Lee for Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree.
而第二名的位置，年复一年，都由布伦达·李的《围绕圣诞树摇摆》夺得。

1048
00:48:13.020 --> 00:48:13.340
Okay.
好吧。

1049
00:48:13.500 --> 00:48:14.300
You know that song?
你知道那首歌吗？

1050
00:48:14.440 --> 00:48:15.100
Yeah, of course.
对，当然知道。

1051
00:48:15.420 --> 00:48:17.740
Well, all of that changed last year.
嗯，这一切在去年改变了。

1052
00:48:18.500 --> 00:48:19.600
Last year?
去年？

1053
00:48:20.280 --> 00:48:29.960
Last year was the 65th anniversary of Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree, and Brenda Lee decided she wanted number one.
去年是《圣诞树周围摇摆》发行65周年，布伦达·李决定她要冲到第一名。

1054
00:48:30.140 --> 00:48:30.980
What'd she do?
她做了什么？

1055
00:48:31.440 --> 00:48:33.120
She went on talk shows.
她上了脱口秀节目。

1056
00:48:33.240 --> 00:48:36.200
She shot a brand new music video for the song.
她为这首歌拍摄了一支全新的音乐录影带。

1057
00:48:36.200 --> 00:48:49.280
She got her own TikTok account and started this whole, like, campaign to make Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree the number one song, finally.
她开了自己的TikTok账号，发起了一场轰轰烈烈的宣传活动，终于要把《圣诞树周围摇摆》推上第一名。

1058
00:48:49.280 --> 00:48:51.700
Like, is there a TikTok dance and the whole thing?
比如，有TikTok舞蹈和那一整套东西吗？

1059
00:48:52.020 --> 00:48:52.680
All the things.
全都有。

1060
00:48:52.680 --> 00:48:53.700
A big trend.
掀起了一股大热潮。

1061
00:48:54.100 --> 00:48:54.340
Yes.
是的。

1062
00:48:54.860 --> 00:49:03.620
To give you a little context, Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree was originally recorded in 1958 when Brenda Lee was only 13 years old.
为了让你了解点背景，《圣诞树周围摇摆》最初录制于1958年，当时布伦达·李年仅13岁。

1063
00:49:03.620 --> 00:49:04.640
Oh, wow.
噢，哇塞。

1064
00:49:04.940 --> 00:49:08.220
She's been, like, at the top of the charts for so long.
她好像在排行榜的顶端待了这么久。

1065
00:49:08.220 --> 00:49:09.620
But never number one.
但从来没拿过第一。

1066
00:49:09.860 --> 00:49:10.140
Never.
从来没有。

1067
00:49:10.540 --> 00:49:10.640
Hmm.
嗯。

1068
00:49:11.040 --> 00:49:11.860
Well, guess what?
好了，你猜怎么着？

1069
00:49:12.500 --> 00:49:14.680
Last year, she did it.
去年，她做到了。

1070
00:49:14.920 --> 00:49:15.540
No way.
不会吧。

1071
00:49:15.540 --> 00:49:16.260
It worked!
成功了！

1072
00:49:16.280 --> 00:49:19.200
She dethroned Mariah Carey!
她把玛丽亚·凯莉拉下了王座！

1073
00:49:19.200 --> 00:49:23.200
Her song hit number one on the Billboard's Top 100.
她的歌登上了公告牌百强单曲榜的第一名。

1074
00:49:23.200 --> 00:49:26.400
It is the oldest song to hit number one.
这是登上榜首历史最悠久的歌曲。

1075
00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:31.520
Brenda Lee became the oldest living person to score a number one song.
布伦达·李成为了获得冠军单曲年龄最大的在世之人。

1076
00:49:31.860 --> 00:49:37.560
And Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree is only the third holiday song to hit number one on the chart.
而且《圣诞树周围摇摆》是榜单上第三首登上榜首的节日歌曲。

1077
00:49:37.880 --> 00:49:39.120
What was the other one?
那另一首是什么？

1078
00:49:39.240 --> 00:49:43.760
The third song is the Chipmunk song by the Chipmunks.
第三首歌是花栗鼠乐队的花栗鼠之歌。

1079
00:49:44.060 --> 00:49:47.280
These other two songs are such great songs.
另外这两首歌都是非常棒的歌。

1080
00:49:47.280 --> 00:49:52.000
Could you imagine being Brenda Lee and being like, that song made it to number one before me?
你能想象自己是布伦达·李，然后心想，那首歌竟然比我先冲到第一名吗？

1081
00:49:53.120 --> 00:49:55.220
Anyway, Brenda Lee, you did it.
总之，布伦达·李，你做到了。

1082
00:49:55.320 --> 00:49:56.540
I am so proud of you.
我为你感到无比骄傲。

1083
00:49:56.840 --> 00:50:03.440
I found an audio clip of her talking about what it's been like to have this Christmas song just enduring over the years.
我找到了一段她的音频剪辑，里面谈到了这首圣诞歌曲历经多年长盛不衰的感受。

1084
00:50:03.440 --> 00:50:05.220
And I want a dust to play it.
我想放给大家听一下。

1085
00:50:05.400 --> 00:50:09.040
Do you and your family listen to your song specifically during the holidays?
你和你的家人在节日期间会专门听你的歌吗？

1086
00:50:09.240 --> 00:50:12.840
Like, surely it has to come on when you're out and about, when you're at the stores.
比如，当你外出、在商店里时，这首歌肯定会放出来吧。

1087
00:50:13.020 --> 00:50:14.900
But, like, do you guys listen to it?
但是，你们会主动去听吗？

1088
00:50:15.220 --> 00:50:15.400
No.
不会。

1089
00:50:15.660 --> 00:50:15.960
No!
不会！

1090
00:50:15.960 --> 00:50:18.400
I mean, if the kids put it on, of course.
我是说，如果孩子们放的话，当然会听。

1091
00:50:18.580 --> 00:50:21.620
But we don't make an effort to put me on.
但我们不会特意去放我的歌。

1092
00:50:21.880 --> 00:50:23.760
They hear enough of me every day.
他们每天听我的声音已经听够了。

1093
00:50:24.400 --> 00:50:33.760
But, no, I'm grateful that, you know, I don't think I'll ever get used to, during the Christmas season,
不过，不，我很感激，你知道的，我想我永远不会习惯在圣诞季里，

1094
00:50:34.020 --> 00:50:38.740
walking into a big department store or something and hearing my song play.
走进一家大型百货公司之类的听到我的歌在播放。

1095
00:50:39.280 --> 00:50:41.780
That's always going to be surreal to me.
对我来说，这总是有一种超现实的感觉。

1096
00:50:43.340 --> 00:50:43.760
Aw.
噢。

1097
00:50:43.760 --> 00:50:44.000
Aw.
噢。

1098
00:50:44.300 --> 00:50:48.060
How old was she when she finally was the number one Christmas song?
当她的歌终于成为冠军圣诞歌曲时，她多大？

1099
00:50:48.360 --> 00:50:48.780
78.
78岁。

1100
00:50:49.280 --> 00:50:49.700
Wow.
哇。

1101
00:50:50.060 --> 00:50:50.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1102
00:50:50.720 --> 00:50:50.940
Yeah.
对。

1103
00:50:50.940 --> 00:50:53.000
And she recorded that when she was 13.
而且她13岁时就录制了这首歌。

1104
00:50:53.340 --> 00:50:54.380
13 years old.
13岁。

1105
00:50:54.620 --> 00:50:55.380
Should we hear it?
我们要听听看吗？

1106
00:50:55.460 --> 00:50:56.140
Let's hear it.
听听吧。

1107
00:50:56.180 --> 00:50:56.820
I think so.
我也这么觉得。

1108
00:50:56.840 --> 00:50:57.320
A little clip of it.
听一小段。

1109
00:50:57.320 --> 00:50:57.600
Yes.
好。

1110
00:51:05.520 --> 00:51:06.480
Yes.
好。

1111
00:51:18.190 --> 00:51:23.770
Rockin' around the Christmas tree, let the Christmas spirit ring.
伴着圣诞树摇摆，让圣诞精神回荡。

1112
00:51:24.770 --> 00:51:29.630
Later we'll have some pumpkin pie and we'll do some...
稍后我们要吃南瓜派，还要做...

1113
00:51:31.740 --> 00:51:32.840
So good, right?
太棒了，对吧？

1114
00:51:33.360 --> 00:51:33.980
13.
13岁。

1115
00:51:34.440 --> 00:51:34.800
13.
13。

1116
00:51:35.240 --> 00:51:35.720
Wow.
哇。

1117
00:51:36.160 --> 00:51:36.480
Yeah.
对。

1118
00:51:36.740 --> 00:51:38.080
That's a great story.
这真是个棒极了的故事。

1119
00:51:38.240 --> 00:51:39.160
I loved that.
我太喜欢了。

1120
00:51:39.480 --> 00:51:45.540
Well, Mariah Carey sent Brenda Lee flowers with a card when she was dethroned and it said this,
玛丽亚·凯莉在榜首位置被取代时，给布兰达·李送了一束花和一张卡片，上面写着：

1121
00:51:46.200 --> 00:51:50.620
Dearest Miss Brenda, congratulations on your historic number one.
亲爱的布兰达女士，祝贺你取得历史性的冠军。

1122
00:51:50.820 --> 00:51:51.960
Have a Merry Christmas.
祝你圣诞快乐。

1123
00:51:52.340 --> 00:51:53.040
Love, Mariah.
爱你的，玛丽亚。

1124
00:51:53.700 --> 00:51:54.440
Classy.
真有风度。

1125
00:51:54.680 --> 00:51:55.420
Classy.
真有风度。

1126
00:51:55.740 --> 00:51:56.180
Yes.
是的。

1127
00:51:56.620 --> 00:51:58.360
Well, that was our holiday bonus episode.
好了，这就是我们的节日特别加更期节目。

1128
00:51:58.360 --> 00:52:00.220
Thanks to the nice folks at Macy's.
感谢梅西百货的好心人们。

1129
00:52:00.380 --> 00:52:04.460
We'll be sharing lots of fun stuff in our Insta stories from today's episode, so be sure
我们会在今天的节目后记中分享许多有趣的内容，所以一定要

1130
00:52:04.460 --> 00:52:05.040
and check them out.
去看看哦。

1131
00:52:05.200 --> 00:52:08.500
And a big thank you to Brian Baumgartner for stopping by the studio.
非常感谢布赖恩·鲍姆加特纳来到我们的演播室。

1132
00:52:08.720 --> 00:52:13.980
We will share where you can get his book, The Night Before Dunder Mifflin, and he's going
我们会分享你在哪里可以买到他的书《唐德·米夫林的前夜》，而且他

1133
00:52:13.980 --> 00:52:18.340
to be joining us again for our episode all about Kevin Malone.
还会再次做客我们关于凯文·马隆的专属节目。

1134
00:52:18.780 --> 00:52:20.400
Please send in your questions.
请踊跃发来你们的问题。

1135
00:52:20.840 --> 00:52:22.940
And next week we have another great episode.
下周我们还有另一期精彩节目。

1136
00:52:22.940 --> 00:52:28.200
We are breaking down a fan favorite, which is the Superfan Hot Girl episode.
我们将剖析粉丝最爱的一集，也就是“辣妹”加长版。

1137
00:52:28.540 --> 00:52:34.260
Yeah, you guys suggested that we break down one of the Superfan episodes, so we re-watched
对，你们建议我们剖析一集加长版节目，所以我们重温了

1138
00:52:34.260 --> 00:52:34.680
Hot Girl.
《辣妹》。

1139
00:52:34.800 --> 00:52:38.700
There were so many great new scenes, and we found so much stuff.
里面有太多精彩的新场景，我们发现了好多料。

1140
00:52:39.100 --> 00:52:42.260
So join us next week for the Hot Girl Superfan episode.
所以请加入我们下周的《辣妹》加长版节目。

1141
00:52:42.260 --> 00:52:43.380
We hope you have a great one.
祝大家过得愉快。

1142
00:52:43.500 --> 00:52:44.000
See you then.
到时见。

1143
00:52:44.340 --> 00:52:53.760
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1144
00:52:54.080 --> 00:52:59.280
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由 Odyssey 出品，由珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1145
00:52:59.280 --> 00:53:01.880
